7.016</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Doessel</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measuring inequality: tools and an illustration</article-title><source>International journal for equity in health</source><year>2006</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>5</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16716217</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1475-9276-5-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hann</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gravelle</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The maldistribution of general practitioners in England and Wales: 1974&#x02013;2003</article-title><source>Br J Gen Pract</source><year>2004</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>894</fpage><lpage>898</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15588532</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Council of Local Authorities for International Relations</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.clair.or.jp/j/forum/series/pdf/fs09-en.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pronovost</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Angus</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Dorman</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Dremsizov</surname><given-names>TT</given-names></name><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physician staffing patterns and clinical outcomes in critically ill patients: a systematic review</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2002</year><volume>288</volume><fpage>2151</fpage><lpage>2162</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12413375</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.288.17.2151</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kahn</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Brake</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Steinberg</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intensivist physician staffing and the process of care in academic medical centres</article-title><source>Quality &#x00026; safety in health care</source><year>2007</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>329</fpage><lpage>333</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17913772</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/qshc.2007.022376</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Ministry of Eucation, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology of Japan</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.mhlw.go.jp/shingi/2008/06/dl/s0618-8a.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Toyabe</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kouhei</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Referral from secondary care and to aftercare in a tertiary care university hospital in Japan</article-title><source>BMC health services research</source><year>2006</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>11</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16503979</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1472-6963-6-11</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Motomatsu</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirata</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Imamura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-grou